    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0824" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">151.096/144: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-14T15:00:00+08:00">November 14, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 15—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>997. Department’s 372, November 12, 6 p.m. Pursuant to suggestion from
                        Gauss,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d678-f1"/> a note along the lines indicated was
                    sent to the Foreign Office October 22; it was tactfully worded and I do not
                    apprehend that it will furnish occasion for repercussion. Copy of note was sent
                    the American Consul under cover of my despatch Number 2412, November 1st.<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d678-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
